{:id :EACL-FORMAL-061
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :benchmark
 :seed-or-trace
 "eacl-explorer/10000-server/user-1/ten-successive-pages"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :performance
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0 commit 34ca6b15039daf8f651dd9ef2ccfb95d483ab112"]
 :affected-backends [:datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "Datomic supplied the engine's private continuation callbacks, but the DataScript and Datahike list entry points used the two-argument engine arity. Public cursors preserved correctness while each later page reopened and replayed the traversal prefix, so work grew with page ordinal."
 :fix
 "Define one adapter-neutral bounded continuation contract, key entries by client/source/schema/query/snapshot lineage, supply it from every list and reverse-list adapter, and use generated continuation decisions to distinguish private resume from authenticated deterministic replay."
 :closing-evidence
 ["AcyclicEngine.DecideAcyclicContinuation"
  "eacl.engine.stable-page-test/lookahead-survives-checkpointing-test"
  "eacl.engine.stable-page-test/cursor-fork-and-idempotence-test"]}
